Abstract Classes
    - use inheritance
    - require classes to use a method blueprint
    - Solid lines in UML Diagram

Interfaces
    - use implementation
    - require classes to use the exact method
    - Dashed lines in UML Diagram

Similarities
    - Can have a subclass implement both
    - subclass can implement multiple interfaces,
    but not multiple inheritance


Inheritance and interfaces are to ways to implement polymorphism (apply same methods
to different types of objects)

Interfaces are good when we just wanted derived classes to have the same methods

